The lowest energy clusters from \textit{n}=4 to \textit{n}=6 have all He atoms on O sites.
In the case of di-vacancy clusters in vanadium, He$_1$V$_2$ in the 1nn configuration is still higher 
in energy than in the 2nn one (Fig.\ref{fig:henv2}) but the difference is reduced to 0.09 eV compared to 0.19 eV 
in the pure vacancy cluster case. 

